                <pb facs="0722" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg708"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No progress was made in the next three meetings on July 18, 22, and 24; telegram
                    231, July 24, from Seoul, reported that the Soviets were recommending a list
                    that omitted 24 rightist parties which claimed a membership of over 15,000,000.
                    (740.00119 Control (Korea)/7–2447) Meanwhile, on July 21, the Soviet delegation
                    issued a lengthy statement to the press in which they argued that a more rapid
                    and successful solution was possible if the two delegations would strictly abide
                    by the Moscow decision and the agreement between the two Foreign Ministers; text
                    of statement was quoted in telegram 225, July 22, from Seoul. (740.00119 Control
                    (Korea)/7–2247)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
